  "idea": "ClickUp vs Monday.com: which all-in-one project tool is less chaotic",
  "text": "Why ClickUp's endless features often lead to team overwhelm and stalled project adoption. Managers spend weeks configuring complex statuses, only to watch employees revert back to disorganized Slack channels. The failure point is cognitive friction when staff get lost inside nested spaces and folders. Streamline operations by disabling unused ClickApps globally or switching client teams to Monday's visual boards. This cuts onboarding friction and keeps sprints running cleanly.",
